---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import FactsRail from "../../components/FactsRail.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Now / Work · Sundharesan Kumaresan" heroOverlay>
  <section class="relative left-1/2 right-1/2 -mx-[50vw] w-screen overflow-hidden bg-fixed bg-cover bg-center" style="min-height:60vh; background-image: linear-gradient(to top, rgba(0,0,0,.72), rgba(0,0,0,.22) 60%, rgba(0,0,0,.42)), url('/img/work.jpg')">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-[1100px] flex-col justify-end px-6 pb-12" style="min-height:60vh; padding-top:7rem;">
      <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-stellar">The present</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-serif font-semibold leading-[0.95] text-white" style="font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 8vw, 5rem);">Now</h1>
    </div>
  </section>
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-[1100px] px-6 py-16">
    <p data-reveal class="max-w-[24ch] font-serif font-semibold leading-[1.05]" style="font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 5vw, 3rem);">I get paid to stare at hard problems until they blink first.</p>
    <div data-reveal class="mt-14 grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-[1.3fr_0.7fr]">
      <div class="max-w-[60ch] space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
        <p>&ldquo;Forward-deployed engineer&rdquo; is the title on paper. In practice it means: you&rsquo;ve got a problem, no plan, and a deadline that was somehow <em>yesterday</em>, and I&rsquo;m the one who shows up. I sit with clients (real humans, real conversations), sketch the fix, draw the architecture, prove it isn&rsquo;t just vibes, then build the whole thing from scratch. Mostly AI. All of it has to survive real users, who are remarkably gifted at breaking things.</p>
        <p>I&rsquo;m an early adopter to a fault. I&rsquo;ll try the shiny new model the week it drops, then spend the next one trying to break it myself, because benchmarks lie and trust is earned. New-age tools, old-school paranoia. Honestly, I treat every build like a story: a problem, some tension, a third act where it finally clicks. My whole job is getting us to that third act: fast, and ideally without the scene where everything&rsquo;s on fire.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:border-l md:border-border md:pl-10 md:sticky md:top-28 md:self-start">
        <FactsRail items={[
          { label: "Role", value: "Forward-deployed engineer (professional problem-haver) · Oogway Labs" },
          { label: "What I build", value: "AI, end to end: from “what if” to “wait, it actually scales”" },
          { label: "How I work", value: "Move fast, break my own ideas first, keep what survives" },
        ]} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
